# Color scheme is locked

Do not change the color scheme, palette, or accent colors unless the user
explicitly asks to change colors.

This includes:

- Backgrounds, borders, text, rings, focus outlines, and hover states
- Amber / gold accents, black glass chrome, and white/neutral text
- Sidebar, search, menus, pills, voice stage, and any other surface
- "Fixing" a layout by swapping in a new color
- Global CSS that restyles buttons, inputs, or focus rings app-wide

If a control needs a size or shape change, keep its existing color classes.

```jsx
// BAD — new colors while fixing layout
className="focus:ring-2 focus:ring-sky-400 bg-amber-400"

// GOOD — same palette, only size/shape changed
className="focus:ring-2 focus:ring-white/30 bg-black/60"
```

When moving or reshaping an existing highlight (for example the voice-stage
speak glow), reuse the same color values. Do not pick a new gold, blue, or
neutral.
